p N1","Starbies","Starbucks Philippines"],"value":"40,990","n":40990,"article":"Starbucks","fact":{"text":"The founders hunted for a name starting with \"st\" and landed on Starbuck, the chief mate in Moby-Dick.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starbucks"}},{"rank":4,"name":"Luckin Coffee","aliases":["Luckin","Ruixing Coffee"],"value":"35,000","n":35000,"article":"Luckin Coffee","fact":{"text":"Delisted in 2020 after its COO faked about US$310 million of sales, it bounced back as China's largest coffee chain.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luckin_Coffee"}},{"rank":5,"name":"Subway","aliases":["Subway sandwich","Doctor's Associates","Subway Sandwiches","Subway restaurant","Subway Restaurants","Pete's Super Sandwiches","Pete's Subway","Doctor's Associates, Inc.","Subway Canada","Pete’s Super Submarines","Subway IP Inc.","Subway India","Subway in India","Subway IP LLC","Subway Sandwich Shops, Inc."],"value":"35,000","n":35000,"article":"Subway (restaurant)","fact":{"text":"Its parent company is Doctor's Associates: the founder hoped the shop would pay his way through medical school.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subway_(restaurant)"}},{"rank":6,"name":"KFC","aliases":["Colonel Sanders' Kentucky Fried Chicken","KFC Corporation","Kentucky Chicken","Kentucky Fried Chicken","KFC company","KFC Arabia","KFC restaurant","KFC Chicken","Kentucky Fried Chicken Corporation","KFC Corp.","Kentucky Fried Chicken Corp.","Kentucky Fried"],"value":"31,981","n":31981,"article":"KFC","fact":{"text":"The name Kentucky Fried Chicken was coined by a sign painter working for its first franchisee, in Utah.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KFC"}},{"rank":7,"name":"Domino's","aliases":["Dominos Pizza","Domino Pizza","Domino Pizza Korea","Dominoes pizza","Dominos Pizza, Inc.","Domino's IP Holder LLC","Domino's IP Holder","Domino's Pizza LLC"],"value":"20,591","n":20591,"article":"Domino's","fact":{"text":"Co-founder Jim Monaghan traded his half of the busines